   "sentenceId": 10,
   "he": "הָאִישׁ נִתְלֶה וְאֵין כּוּ׳. מַאי טַעְמָא — אָמַר קְרָא: ״וְתָלִיתָ אוֹתוֹ עַל עֵץ״, אוֹתוֹ וְלֹא אוֹתָהּ.",
   "en": "The mishna states: «A man is hanged, but» a woman is «not» hanged. The Gemara asks: «What is the reason» for this? «The verse states:» “And if a man has committed a sin worthy of death, and he is put to death, «and you shall hang him on a tree”» (Deuteronomy 21:22). The verse indicates that one should hang «“him,”» a man, «but not her,» a woman."
  }
